Article 21 In rural areas without the conditions for centralized disposal of medical waste, medical and health institutions shall, in accordance with the requirements of the competent health administrative department and the competent environmental protection administrative department of the people's government at the county level, dispose of the medical waste generated by themselves on site. Where medical waste is disposed of on site, the following basic requirements shall be met:
(1) Disposable medical instruments after use and medical waste that may easily cause injury shall be disinfected and deactivated;
(2) Medical waste that can be incinerated shall be incinerated in a timely manner;
(3) Medical waste that cannot be incinerated shall be disinfected and then buried in a centralized landfill.

Article 23 A centralized medical waste disposal unit shall meet the following conditions:
(1) Having medical waste storage and disposal facilities or equipment that meet the requirements of environmental protection and hygiene;
(2) Having trained technical personnel and corresponding skilled workers;
(3) Having institutions and personnel responsible for testing and evaluating the effectiveness of medical waste disposal;
(4) Having rules and regulations to ensure the safe disposal of medical waste.

Article 39 When performing their supervision and inspection duties, the competent administrative departments of health and the competent administrative departments of environmental protection shall have the authority to take the following measures:
(1) Conduct on-site inspections of relevant units, understand the situation, carry out on-site monitoring, and investigate and collect evidence;
(2) Consult or copy relevant materials on medical waste management, and collect samples;
(3) Order entities and individuals that violate the provisions of these Regulations to cease illegal acts;
(4) Seal or temporarily seize premises, equipment, means of transport, and articles suspected of violating the provisions of these Regulations;
(5) Investigate and handle acts violating the provisions of these Regulations.

Article 45 If a medical and health institution or a centralized medical waste disposal unit, in violation of these Regulations, falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent administrative department of health or the competent administrative department of environmental protection of the local people's government at or above the county level shall, within their respective functions and duties, order it to make corrections within a specified time limit and give a warning; if it fails to make corrections within the specified time limit, a fine of not less than 2,000 yuan but not more than 5,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) failing to establish or improve a medical waste management system, or failing to set up a monitoring department or full-time (or part-time) personnel;
(2) failing to provide training on relevant laws and professional technologies, safety protection, and emergency handling to relevant personnel;
(3) failing to take occupational health protection measures for personnel engaged in the collection, transportation, storage, and disposal of medical waste and management personnel;
(4) failing to register medical waste or failing to keep registration records;
(5) failing to disinfect and clean used medical waste transport tools or transport vehicles at designated places in a timely manner;
(6) failing to collect and transport medical waste in a timely manner;
(7) failing to regularly test and evaluate the environmental pollution prevention and hygiene effects of medical waste disposal facilities, or failing to archive and report the test and evaluation results.

Article 46 If a medical and health institution or a centralized medical waste disposal unit, in violation of these Regulations, falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent administrative department of health or the competent administrative department of environmental protection of the local people's government at or above the county level shall, within their respective functions and duties, order it to make corrections within a specified time limit, give a warning, and may concurrently impose a fine of not more than 5,000 yuan; if it fails to make corrections within the specified time limit, a fine of not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 30,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) the storage facilities or equipment do not meet the requirements for environmental protection and hygiene;
(2) failing to place medical waste in special packaging or containers according to categories;
(3) failing to use standard special vehicles to transport medical waste or using vehicles for transporting medical waste to transport other items;
(4) failing to install online pollutant emission monitoring devices or the monitoring devices are not constantly in normal operation.

Article 47 If a medical and health institution or a centralized medical waste disposal unit falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent administrative department of health or the competent administrative department of environmental protection of the local people's government at or above the county level shall, within their respective functions and duties, order it to make corrections within a specified time limit, give a warning, and concurrently impose a fine of not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 10,000 yuan; if it fails to make corrections within the specified time limit, a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 30,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the act causes a communicable disease transmission or environmental pollution accident, the original licensing department shall temporarily withhold or revoke the practice license or business license; if the act constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) discarding medical waste during transportation, dumping or piling up medical waste in non-storage sites, or mixing medical waste with other waste or domestic garbage;
(2) failing to implement the hazardous waste transfer manifest management system;
(3) handing over medical waste to units or individuals that have not obtained a business license for collection, transportation, storage, or disposal;
(4) the disposal of medical waste does not comply with the national standards and specifications for environmental protection and hygiene;
(5) failing to strictly disinfect sewage or excrement of patients with communicable diseases or suspected patients with communicable diseases in accordance with these Regulations, or discharging them into the sewage treatment system without meeting the national discharge standards;
(6) failing to manage and dispose of domestic garbage generated by hospitalized patients with communicable diseases or suspected patients with communicable diseases as medical waste.
